  pageIndex: 5
  pageTitle: Payloads
  leftPageBody: "Payloads:\r\nThe payload is the actual data being carried inside
    the packet\u2014the \u201Cmessage content\u201D being delivered. In TCP, payloads
    are split across multiple packets and reassembled by the receiver. Suspicious
    payloads might contain unexpected data, corrupted formatting, or content that
    does not match the expected communication type."
